Dear Terrence,
Thank you so much.
Please find below my syntax. In summary, I want to look at the effect of fishery income (LnF.income) on child development. There are three types of child development indicators: gross motor (GMcum.score), personal social (PScum.score), and communication (COMcum.score). So, I want to look at the effect of fishery income (LnF.income) on each of these indicator. The number suffix at the end of the variable names represent the time points (.6, .12, .18, .24).
In  addition, I would also like to see the effect of fishery income on child development that goes through the nutrition pathway (represented by the zha mediating variable).
To take advantage of the longitudinal nature of the data, I would like to apply the method described in Allison et al. 2017 (Maximum likelihood for cross-lagged panel models with fixed effects) published in SOCIUS.

Your idea about splitting the "big" model into smaller models sounds interesting. Perhaps, I can do that and if the patterns in the smaller models are similar to those in the big models, that may mean that the big model is not so bad. Does that sound a reasonable approach?

Any advice you can provide will be appreciated.

Many thanks,

Ranaivo

med_mod <- '

# FISHING INCOME TO ZHA

# Define the latent fixed effects

alpha =~ zha.12 + zha.24

# Regressions

zha.12 ~ a*LnF.income.6   + b*Breastfed.6   + c*ChildHealth.6    + d*FS.score.6   + e*MotherHealth.6   + f*zha.6   + g*LnPCExp.6
zha.24 ~ a*LnF.income.18 + b*Breastfed.18 + c*ChildHealth.18 + d*FS.score.18 + e*MotherHealth.18 + f*zha.18 + g*LnPCExp.18

# Pre-determined variables

zha.12 ~~ ChildHealth.18 + zha.18 + MotherHealth.18

# Alpha (fixed effect) correlated with time-varying variables (implementation of the fixed effects)

alpha ~~ LnF.income.6 + LnF.income.18 + Breastfed.6 + Breastfed.18 + ChildHealth.6  + ChildHealth.18 +
                 FS.score.6 + FS.score.18 + MotherHealth.6 + MotherHealth.18 + zha.6 + zha.18 + LnPCExp.6 + LnPCExp.18

# Free error variance of the outcome variable

zha.12 ~~ zha.12
zha.24 ~~ zha.24

# FISHING INCOME TO GROSS MOTOR CONTROLLING FOR ZHA

# Define the latent fixed effects

alpha1 =~ GMcum.score.12 + GMcum.score.24 + PScum.score.12 + PScum.score.24 + COMcum.score.12 + COMcum.score.24

# Regressions

GMcum.score.12 ~ a1*LnF.income.6  +  b1*Age.months.6  + c1*Breastfed.6  + d1*ChildHealth.6  + e1*FS.score.6  + f1*MotherHealth.6  + g1*GMcum.score.6  + h1*Stunted.6  +
                                   k1*zha.12 + j1*LnPCExp.6
GMcum.score.24 ~ a1*LnF.income.18 +  b1*Age.months.18 + c1*Breastfed.18 + d1*ChildHealth.18 + e1*FS.score.18 + f1*MotherHealth.18 + g1*GMcum.score.18 + h1*Stunted.18 +
                                    k1*zha.24 + j1*LnPCExp.18

# Pre-determined variables

GMcum.score.12 ~~ ChildHealth.18 + MotherHealth.18 + GMcum.score.18

# FISHING INCOME TO PERSONAL SOCIAL CONTROLLING FOR ZHA

