You're still talking about mean-centering the covariates, right? Not x and y? Because that wouldn't be called for.

If you're only mean-centering covariates, it's possible the issue is that centering works differently for multilevel models (which you didn't mention before).There's an entire literature on the implications of different centering strategies for multilevel data.

