Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

> Is there a way to build DYMIMIC model with "lavaan" package?

Without reading the source, I doubt it.  lavaan considers parameters fixed, so other dynamic models are not possible, neither are models such as MNLFA.  Random intercepts (and eventually slopes) are only possible in the context of MLSEM.  Random-intercept cross-lagged panel models <https://ellenhamaker.github.io/RI-CLPM/lavaan.html> are possible only because data are in wide format.

Terrence D. Jorgensen
Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics
Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam
http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen

